# N3 example: builtin-call-complete.
# Companion to builtin-call-complete.eye: exercises absolute value,
# exponentiation (used as a square root via a 0.5 exponent, since N3 has
# no dedicated sqrt builtin), list length, and list sorting -- the same
# small set of builtins the .eye companion's `summary/4` exercises (a much
# narrower smoke test than the .srl companion's full BuiltInCall-grammar
# sweep, which N3 has no equivalent surface for).

@prefix math: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/math#>.
@prefix list: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/list#>.
@prefix : <http://example/>.

:numbers :values (-3.7 7 2).

{:numbers :values ?values.
 -3.7 math:absoluteValue ?absolute.
 (9 0.5) math:exponentiation ?root.
 ?values list:length ?count.
 ?values list:sort ?sorted.
} => {:summary :absolute ?absolute; :root ?root; :count ?count; :sorted ?sorted}.
